Subject: Wifi: tell the runner the RX channel

ndsrecomp modification to vendored melonDS src/Wifi.cpp (GPLv3 5(a)
notice; see patches/README.md for the convention).

CheckRX passes CurChannel to the runner hook
nds_wifi_local_mp_note_rx_channel right before each regular
MP_RecvPacket. The runner uses it to hand over a replayed lobby beacon only
on the channel the guest is scanning; CheckRX itself drops frames from
other channels, as before. The hook only stores the value.

--- a/src/Wifi.cpp
+++ b/src/Wifi.cpp
@@ (runner hook declarations)
+void nds_wifi_local_mp_note_rx_channel(int channel);
@@ Wifi::CheckRX, type 0
         if (type == 0)
         {
+            ::nds_wifi_local_mp_note_rx_channel(CurChannel);
             rxlen = Platform::MP_RecvPacket(RXBuffer, &timestamp, NDS.UserData);
